---
description: Standard UI layout patterns (v0-style)
alwaysApply: true
---

All UI must follow predictable SaaS-style layout patterns.

Do not invent new layout structures unless explicitly requested.

---

# Page Layout Pattern

All pages must follow this structure:

Page
 ├ PageHeader
 │   ├ Title
 │   └ Actions
 │
 └ Content
     └ Card
         └ Feature Content

Rules:
- PageHeader contains page title and primary actions
- Main content must be wrapped inside Card components
- Avoid multiple nested containers
- Maintain clear visual hierarchy

---

# List Page Pattern

Standard layout for list views:

PageHeader
Toolbar (filters / search / quick actions)

Card
 └ Table or list content

List pages should include:
- search or filter toolbar (if applicable)
- row actions via DropdownMenu
- loading state
- empty state

---

# Detail Page Pattern

Standard layout for entity details:

PageHeader
Card
 ├ Section 1
 ├ Section 2
 └ Section 3

Rules:
- group related fields into sections
- avoid long unstructured layouts
- keep spacing consistent

---

# Create / Edit Pattern

Entity editing must use:

Sheet
 └ Form

Rules:
- prefer Sheet instead of full-page forms
- group related fields
- keep form sections clear and readable

---

# Interaction Patterns

Use consistent interaction rules:

Create / Edit
→ Sheet

Delete / Destructive action
→ Dialog confirmation

Row actions
→ DropdownMenu

Navigation
→ Buttons or links in PageHeader

Avoid inventing new interaction paradigms.

---

# Visual Simplicity

UI should follow a minimal SaaS style:

- clean layouts
- generous spacing
- limited color usage
- avoid visual noise

Prefer clarity over decorative design.

---

# Component Reuse

Always prefer existing components from:

components/ui/
components/

Do not duplicate UI primitives.
Extend existing components when possible.
